Package: pve-rclone-backup
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: ariedotcodotnz <ariedotcodotnz@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libpve-storage-perl (>= 9.0.13), libjson-perl, perl, zstd, tar, gzip
Recommends: pve-manager (>= 9.0), pve-qemu-kvm
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/ariedotcodotnz/pve-rclone-backup
Description: Offsite replication of Proxmox VE backups through rclone
 pve-rclone-backup replicates finished vzdump backups from local storage to
 cloud storage supported by rclone (Microsoft OneDrive first), encrypted and
 in resumable segments, without a second local copy. A storage plugin of type
 rclone-backup lists the offsite backups in Proxmox VE, with notes,
 protection, offsite retention and the guest configuration.
 .
 The package contains the pve-rclone-backupd daemon, the pve-rclone-backup
 command line and terminal interface, and the Perl storage plugin.
